            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A medical device comprises a plurality of electrode nodes, each electrode node is configured to be coupled to an electrode configured to contact a patient's tissue. A medical device further comprises a control circuitry which is configured to use one or more of the plurality of electrodes as stimulating electrodes to provide stimulation to the patient's neural tissue. A control circuitry is further configured to use one or more of the plurality of electrodes as sensing electrodes to sense neural responses evoked by the stimulation. A control circuitry is further configured to determine at least one feature of the sensed neural responses, upon detection of a change in the at least one feature: determining a likelihood for each of a plurality of events that could be responsible for the change in the at least one feature, and selecting the event with the highest likelihood. A control circuitry is further configured to adjust the stimulation based on the selected event.</p>
            </abstract>
